From f7004c9ffa38d6a3976a542b73278db0902e054d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:35:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] aeraui: a shared file picker, with Telegram as its
 first caller

Telegram's "Attach a file" overlay was AERA's only file picker, written
inside telegram_scene.cpp: one file, four hard-coded storage roots, a
synchronous opendir capped at 300 entries, and the overlay rebuilt on
every folder change. Anything else that needs the user to pick a file
had to copy it.

Move it to components/file_picker as a picker any scene can open:

- Modes: one file, several files, a folder, or a name to save as (with
  Files' name dialog and a confirmation before replacing a file).
- Browsing follows Files: it starts in the current storage, Parent
  folder goes up to /, and Storage and Root jump to a volume or the
  root. Hidden files follow the Files preference.
- A caller can confine it to storage roots instead. Telegram does, with
  its worker's four roots, and links are then skipped, so Telegram
  behaves as before.
- Folders are listed on a worker thread and shown 100 rows at a time as
  in Files; picture thumbnails are decoded lazily as Telegram did.
- Extension filters, a starting folder, and a path length limit for
  callers that pass the path on in a fixed-size message.

The folder model (List, Parent, Allowed) is in file_picker_list.cpp,
without LVGL, and tests/file_picker_test.cpp covers it.

